Complete local Java example; the app itself does not execute it:
```java
import java.util.List;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;
public class Main {

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    var groups = List.of("oak", "elm", "pine").stream()
        .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(String::length, Collectors.counting()));
    System.out.println(groups.getOrDefault(3, 0L));
  }
}
```

after:
Group the words by length, then read the count for length three. The L in 0L makes the fallback a long, matching the count type.

